---
description: Run npm and npx without the Windows PowerShell shim
alwaysApply: true
---

On Windows, do not invoke `npm` or `npx` directly from PowerShell. PowerShell resolves those names to `npm.ps1` and `npx.ps1`, which fail when script execution is disabled.

Use the project launchers. They call `npm.cmd` / `npx.cmd` and do not change the execution policy.

- `node scripts/npm.mjs <args>`
- `node scripts/npx.mjs <args>`
- `node scripts/check-package-bin.mjs` to verify the launcher

On macOS and Linux, `npm` and `npx` are unchanged. Node scripts that spawn a package manager must use `scripts/lib/resolve-bin.mjs`.
